id: pm-z0cfor
title: "Floor polarity for the tracker measurement ratchet, with graph edge and node floors declared"
description: "Add the second polarity to the tracker measurement ratchet so a declaration can guard a property whose good direction is up, and declare the first two floors.\n\nDelivered in scripts/release/tracker-measurement-gate.mjs: a `resolveDeclaredBound` helper that accepts exactly one of `ceiling` or `floor` and refuses zero or both; a `bound_polarity_not_declared` refusal for an ambiguous declaration and a `floor_not_a_count` refusal mirroring the existing ceiling check; `floor_undercut` and `within_floor` evaluation reasons; a floor branch in the re-baseline path that takes the maximum of declared and observed so a floor rises toward observation and is never lowered; a violation line that names its polarity and renders the shortfall as a negative distance; and a negative control that now proves both polarities fail, because a control that exercises one direction leaves the other a hypothesis.\n\nContributor attribution is deliberately restricted to ceiling violations. Contributor rows are read from the record as it stands, so they can name the mutations that pushed a population past a ceiling and can never name rows that were deleted below a floor. Claiming otherwise would be the more useful-looking behaviour and would be wrong.\n\nTwo floors declared in scripts/release/tracker-measurements.json: total deduplicated directed relationship edges, owned by pm-96h7, and total graph nodes, owned by pm-o2kc. Both were baselined from the gate's own commit view via --update at 11,318 edges and 2,368 nodes."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: "area:ci",gate,governance,measurement
created_at: "2026-08-07T17:21:22.188Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-07T17:21:38.661Z"
