completed_at: "2026-08-07T17:21:38.596Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "A declaration may carry a floor, and an observed value below it fails the gate with a distinct reason; The re-baseline path raises a floor and never lowers it, mirroring the ceiling path in the opposite direction; The negative control proves both a ceiling violation and a floor violation fail; Total deduplicated directed edges and total graph nodes are declared as floors from a commit-view measurement"
parent: pm-g4k74y
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "The ratchet now enforces two directions. scripts/release/tracker-measurement-gate.mjs gained resolveDeclaredBound, the bound_polarity_not_declared and floor_not_a_count refusals, floor_undercut and within_floor reasons, a Math.max re-baseline branch for floors, a polarity-naming violation line, and a negative control that proves both directions fail. scripts/release/tracker-measurements.json declares graph-profile-edges-floor at 11,318 owned by pm-96h7 and graph-profile-nodes-floor at 2,368 owned by pm-o2kc, both baselined from the gate's own commit view."
expected_result: "A declaration guarding a property whose good direction is up fails when the property falls, and re-baselining cannot be used to accept the regression."
actual_result: "Verified locally: the dual negative control reports ceiling_exceeded at declared 0 observed 1 and floor_undercut at declared floor 2 observed 1, and exits 0 only when both fire. The full check passes with 26 enforced and 0 retired over 2,365 items in a commit view of 6,025 committable files. The spec runs 46 tests green at 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines over the gate script."
